From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:03:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Stop firing alarms when none are left

After the last alarm fired the loop looked at the first alarm of the
empty list, which crashes with libc++, like on the first OSSleepTicks.
---
 src/Cafe/OS/libs/coreinit/coreinit_Alarm.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Cafe/OS/libs/coreinit/coreinit_Alarm.cpp b/src/Cafe/OS/libs/coreinit/coreinit_Alarm.cpp
index ae2d1e6..1e2b051 100644
--- a/src/Cafe/OS/libs/coreinit/coreinit_Alarm.cpp
+++ b/src/Cafe/OS/libs/coreinit/coreinit_Alarm.cpp
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@ namespace coreinit
 			}
 #endif
 			// debug end
-			while (true)
+			while (!g_activeAlarmList.empty())
 			{
 				auto firstAlarm = g_activeAlarmList.begin();
 				if (currentTick >= (*firstAlarm)->m_nextFire)
